    "body": "Yeah, having the unlevelled URL point to the (delta-spec) Overflow 4 is a mistake; we'll fix, so the URL will go back to working.\r\n\r\nThat said, the unlevelled URLs are for humans, not deep-linking; their content can and does change. It so happens that properties (and many other definitions) use a particular ID pattern that is not likely to change across levels, but this isn't something you should particularly depend on.  We do not have a generic mechanism (yet) to link to \"the latest version of the definition for a property X\". (But creating such a mechanism, built on top of the Bikeshed linking mechanism, would be easy and probably quite useful.)\r\n\r\nSo you really should be linking to `/css-overflow-3` for this, not `/css-overflow`.",
