    "body": "> So you really should be linking to `/css-overflow-3` for this, not `/css-overflow`.\r\n\r\nOK, that’s what the change in this PR branch does. So I guess it’s the right change.\r\n\r\nBut it remains unclear to me what happens later if/when `/css-overflow-3` becomes completely superseded or obsolete and is no longer being maintained and shouldn’t be used by implementors.\r\n\r\nIt seems like at that point we’d need to go back into the HTML spec and (re)update the reference to point to whatever the current spec is that implementors should be using. And it’s also unclear to me how we are to know _when_ things have changed with the status of that spec version that it’s necessary to do (re)change the reference.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
