    "updated_at": "2017-09-28T01:42:59Z",
    "body": "> That said, the unlevelled URLs are for humans, not deep-linking; their content can and does change.\r\n\r\nDoesn’t the content of the leveled URLs change too? Or at least the _status_ of them changes to the point that eventually implementors should not be using them any longer, right?\r\n\r\nI mean, it seems like the leveled URLs eventually become superseded by a later version of the same content, and when that happens, implementors should no longer be using the older leveled version but should instead by using the newer one that has superseded it.\r\n\r\nAnd so also at that time, the HTML spec should no longer be referencing the older leveled version but should be changed to reference whatever newer version has superseded it.",
